# Local development secrets. Copy to `.env.local` and fill in.
#
# Wrangler loads `.env.local` *instead of* `.env` files when it exists, so this
# file has to carry every secret the Worker needs, including the auth ones.
#
# The Deploy to Cloudflare button reads this file too and asks for every
# uncommented line as a required secret, so only the required ones are live here.

# Better Auth ------------------------------------------------------------
# Any long random string: `openssl rand -hex 32`.
BETTER_AUTH_SECRET=

# Secret storage ---------------------------------------------------------
# Required. Any passphrase; it is SHA-256'd into an AES-256-GCM key that
# encrypts environment variables and provider API keys at rest. Changing it
# makes every stored secret unreadable, so set it once per instance.
# In production: `wrangler secret put ENCRYPTION_KEY`.
ENCRYPTION_KEY=

# Optional ---------------------------------------------------------------
# Uncomment what you need.
#
# Pin the public origin only if the app sits behind a proxy that rewrites the
# Host header. Left unset, the origin is read from each request.
# BETTER_AUTH_URL=
#
# LLM provider keys. A key set here wins over anything saved in the admin
# console, and the console refuses to manage a provider that a secret already
# covers. Workers AI needs no key; it runs through the `AI` binding. On a
# deployed instance, add keys from the admin console instead.
# ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=
# OPENAI_API_KEY=
# GOOGLE_API_KEY=
